{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And every raven.</b> This too is not that which is called corbeil, for they examined the corbeil and found that it has an extra toe and a crop, and if so it is a predator — if it is the raven, since in אלו טרפות it explains that in the raven there are only two signs of purity, for it is among the twenty-four unclean birds, and if it is not a predator it would have three signs of purity. Rather, certainly it is a predator, and if so, how can it say there that a bird that comes before us with two signs is pure, provided one recognizes the raven — and if it resembles a raven and one also recognizes the raven, how is it pure, given that we say the raven is a predator, and we hold that any predatory bird is impure? Rather, certainly that which we call corbeil is not the raven of Scripture, but rather that which is seen spitting at the time of mating is certainly the raven."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:58.490871783Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}